  "rulings": {
    "references": [
      {
        "link": "https://world.digimoncard.com/rule/?card_no=BT1-089#qaResult_card",
        "num": 1,
        "text": "Official English Q&A for BT1-089 (Mar. 28, 2024)"
      },
      {
        "link": "https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/930985633109934090/939058138525630484/unknown.png",
        "num": 2,
        "text": "English Carddass Email: Mimi Tachikawa BT1-089 Optional or Mandatory (Feb. 4, 2022)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "You can resolve their effects in any order. For example, if you're starting the turn at 1 memory, you can resolve this card's effect first to go up to 3 memory, then activate [ST2-12 Matt Ishida]'s effect to go to 4 memory and above.",
        "question": "I have both this card and [ST2-12 Matt Ishida] in play. How do I activate their effects?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Like Main effects on Option cards, you can activate these effects at any time during your main phase. However, you can't activate them to interrupt an attack or another effect.",
        "question": "What timing does [Main] occur at?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, Digimon in breeding areas aren't checked by this effect.",
        "question": "Can I use this card's Main effect if I have a level 5 or higher green Digimon in my Breeding Area?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it does. Unless otherwise specified, cards don't lose their effects when suspended.",
        "question": "Does this card's Start of Your Turn effect activate if it is suspended?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you can. Hatching Digimon and moving them to the battle area doesn't count as playing them, so you can attack with them immediately.",
        "question": "During my breeding phase, I hatch a level 2 Digimon from my Digi-Egg deck. I then digivolve that Digimon into a level 3 Digimon during my main phase. If I use this card's effect to move that Digimon to my battle area, can I attack with it immediately?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "While it is possible, this can only be done if you have a Level 2 Digimon in your Breeding Area. If you have a Digimon that can be moved out from the Breeding Area it must be moved out. If you have no Digimon in your Breeding Area and cards in your Digi-Egg deck, you must hatch.",
        "question": "Is it possible to suspend this tamer with its [Main] effect and not use its effect?",
        "reference": "[2]"
      }
    ]
  },
